2. The following are the salient features of the Bill-
(1) to provide that all the seats in the corporation to be filled up by direct election, from divisions and wards of the
respective municipal corporations.
(2) to provide for representation in the respective councils of-
(a) persons having special knowledge or experience in municipal administration, without voting rights;
(b) the members of the House of the People and the members of the Tamil Nadu Legislative Assembly representing
constituencies which comprise wholly or partly within the area of the respective corporations ;
(c) the members of the Council of States registered as electors within the area of the respective corporations;
(d) the Chairpersons of the Committees who arc not councillors (other than the wards committees) constituted under the
respective Acts;
(3) (a) to provide for reservation of scats for members of the Scheduled Castes and the Scheduled Tribes in proportion
to their population in the cities and that one-third of the seats so reserved be reserved for women belonging to the
Scheduled Castes and the Scheduled Tribes;
(b) to provide that one-third of the total number of seats in the council to be filled by direct election (including the seats
reserved for women belonging to the Scheduled Castes and the Scheduled Tribes) be reserved for women;

The Government have therefore now decided to amend the Tamil Nadu District Municipalities Act, 1920 (Tamil Nadu Act
